<title>NEW ZEALAND: DB Group lifts year profit by 75 percent.</title>
<headline>DB Group lifts year profit by 75 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year result to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   30.37 vs 17.34</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    9.2 vs 5.7</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			    2.0 vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Turnover			     650.4 vs 658.3</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 47.1 vs 45.1</p>
<p>    Tax				     15.6 vs 25.6</p>
<p>    Equity earnings		     0.26 vs 0.03</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credits.</p>
<p>Pay date  February 2</p>
<p>Reg date  January 31</p>
<p>Note - DB Group Ltd is a brewing company 59.8 percent owned by Asia Pacific Breweries Ltd, a venture between Heineken NV and Fraser and Neave Ltd.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
